{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20316",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.68,
      "end_seconds": 6.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.87,
      "text": "Doctor, this one's ready for you. Everything's on the chart, but I'll go through it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.44,
      "end_seconds": 11.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "So, thank you. Right, hello, what's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.1,
      "end_seconds": 16.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "Well, I've been having tingling in my feet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.48,
      "end_seconds": 24.42,
      "duration_seconds": 6.94,
      "text": "Right, when was the first time you noticed it? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.8,
      "end_seconds": 31.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Yeah, it's been three weeks now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.11,
      "end_seconds": 35.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "How strong would you say it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.53,
      "end_seconds": 39.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "A three out of ten, I suppose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.01,
      "end_seconds": 45.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Have you had a dull ache after the cramp?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.83,
      "end_seconds": 64.64,
      "duration_seconds": 17.81,
      "text": "Yes, about the same, two months. As for dull ache after the cramp, I'd give it a six, out of ten. And, And there's cramps in my calves at night as well, nearly five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.46,
      "end_seconds": 88.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.13,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.29,
      "end_seconds": 101.8,
      "duration_seconds": 11.51,
      "text": "Um, um, yes, diclofenac. I've no idea what the reaction was, only that I'm not supposed to have it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.05,
      "end_seconds": 105.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.6,
      "end_seconds": 112.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "It's valsartan, 80 milligrams, once a day for my blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.18,
      "end_seconds": 115.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "And for how long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.62,
      "end_seconds": 118.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "For two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.27,
      "end_seconds": 121.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.92,
      "end_seconds": 129.93,
      "duration_seconds": 7.01,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure, for five years. I have diabetes, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.47,
      "end_seconds": 136.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.34,
      "end_seconds": 146.4,
      "duration_seconds": 9.06,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. I live with my elderly mother. I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.56,
      "end_seconds": 163.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.53,
      "end_seconds": 170.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.23,
      "text": "Just keyhole surgery on my gallbladder, two years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.68,
      "end_seconds": 176.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Any chest pain, redness of the leg or shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.7,
      "end_seconds": 180.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "No, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.51,
      "end_seconds": 185.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "What about back pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.72,
      "end_seconds": 187.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "No. No back pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.83,
      "end_seconds": 194.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.36,
      "end_seconds": 198.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Oh, no, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.99,
      "end_seconds": 202.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Any trouble with the waterworks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.77,
      "end_seconds": 205.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Oh, no, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 210.53,
      "end_seconds": 221.24,
      "duration_seconds": 10.71,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. BP is 112 over 80, respiratory rate 18, temperature is 36.8 degrees, pulse 86, oxygen saturation is 98 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.16,
      "end_seconds": 223.86,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.57,
      "end_seconds": 230.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.59,
      "end_seconds": 233.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.47,
      "end_seconds": 255.79,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "Both calves are soft and not tender, and the pulses at your feet are good."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.92,
      "end_seconds": 260.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "All finished, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.38,
      "end_seconds": 284.72,
      "duration_seconds": 7.34,
      "text": "So where does that leave us? I'd lean towards night-time muscle cramps without a worrying cause."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.49,
      "end_seconds": 288.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.92,
      "end_seconds": 318.46,
      "duration_seconds": 28.54,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like night-time muscle cramps without a worrying cause, but I'd like to confirm. I'm sending you for a blood sugar test because of tingling feet. I'm sending you for blood tests because of muscle cramps. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.4,
      "end_seconds": 326.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "When would that take place?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.04,
      "end_seconds": 347.23,
      "duration_seconds": 19.19,
      "text": "Keep well hydrated through the day. Keep an eye out, and if one leg becomes red, hot or swollen, call us the same day or go to emergency. Let's review you in four weeks. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 347.79,
      "end_seconds": 352.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "Mm, uh, okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.38,
      "end_seconds": 356.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ]
}